---
/* SEO Aberdeen: the site's main SEO landing page (position ~15-17 for
   "seo aberdeen" on the live site, Nov 2026).

   Copy, title and description are ported from the live Webflow page
   (www.yannhamonou.com/marketing-services/seo-aberdeen, 18 Nov 2026) so the
   migration does not halve the page that ranks. Only typos were fixed.
   Edit the copy here; keep the h1 "SEO Aberdeen". */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Container from '../../components/ui/Container.astro';
import Heading from '../../components/ui/Heading.astro';
import Text from '../../components/ui/Text.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';
import Tag from '../../components/ui/Tag.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/ui/Icon.astro';
import ContactForm from '../../components/ContactForm.astro';
import { serviceImages } from '../../data/index';
import { getServices } from '../../lib/keystatic';

const services = await getServices();
const otherServices = services.filter((s) => s.slug !== 'seo-aberdeen');
const origin = new URL('/', Astro.site).origin;

const results = [
  {
    client: 'Arnlea Systems',
    body: 'Aberdeen-based Arnlea Systems went from invisible on Google to ranking #2 and eventually #1 for "ATEX inspection software" and other related inquiries within weeks of a Webflow rebuild and SEO/GEO strategy.',
    quote: '"Inbound enquiries are now a primary source of pipeline." Claire Murray, Head of Business Development',
    href: '/work/arnlea/',
    linkLabel: 'Read the Arnlea case study',
  },
  {
    client: 'Bowtie Master from Salus-Technical',
    body: 'A full SEO/GEO audit revealing flaws at the structural, technical and content level. Still ongoing but SEO visibility jumped from "nowhere to be seen" to rank 1 to 5 for targeted keywords a week into the project.',
    href: '/work/BowtieMaster/',
    linkLabel: 'Read the BowtieMaster case study',
  },
  {
    client: 'Viewport3',
    body: 'Here, I started with positioning to get a detailed understanding of the context and environment. This was extremely helpful to develop an SEO strategy that eventually delivered first places for the target keywords we selected. The company is now routinely mentioned in AI answers when the topic of dimensional assurance and subsea photogrammetry match the user requests.',
    href: '/work/viewport3/',
    linkLabel: 'Read the Viewport3 case study',
  },
];

const reasons = [
  { title: 'Local and global knowledge', body: 'I understand the Aberdeen market (the energy transition, the growing tech sector, the competitive professional services market) and how local and global businesses compete for visibility online.' },
  { title: 'Proven expertise', body: 'Years of experience in SEO, content strategy, and digital marketing. Demonstrated GEO results.' },
  { title: 'Flexible and transparent', body: 'No cookie-cutter packages, just clear strategies that deliver.' },
  { title: 'Future proofed for AI-search', body: "Whilst consultants and agencies still optimise for Google alone, I also optimise for how AI engines decide which businesses to cite and recommend, so your visibility doesn't disappear as search behaviour shifts." },
];

const offer = [
  { title: 'Local & global SEO', body: 'Your business needs to appear when customers search for your services. I optimise Google Business Profiles, local citations, and content to drive visibility in local search results, and build the domain authority needed to compete nationally and internationally.' },
  { title: 'Technical SEO', body: 'I audit your website to fix issues that stop you ranking. From site speed and indexing to structured data, I ensure search engines can crawl and understand your site.' },
  { title: 'Content & On-Page SEO', body: 'Pages that rank and convert. I optimise copy, headings, metadata and internal linking around the terms your buyers actually search for, written so both search engines and AI models can pull out and cite what matters.' },
  { title: 'Link Building & Authority', body: 'Through ethical outreach and local partnerships, I help build the authority your website needs to compete with bigger players.' },
  { title: 'Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO)', body: "Google's AI Overviews and AI Mode, ChatGPT, Perplexity and Gemini are increasingly where your buyers start their research. Google builds its AI answers from its normal search index, so the groundwork is good SEO. On top of that, I structure each page to answer the follow-up questions these tools ask, in sections that still make sense when quoted on their own, and I work on getting your business named on the third-party sites AI answers draw from. I don't sell llms.txt files or \"AI schema\" as a fix: Google has said its AI features don't need them." },
  { title: 'SEO & GEO audit', body: "A one-off assessment of your website's performance across both traditional search and AI answer engines. You get a detailed report with prioritised actions: technical fixes, content gaps, schema improvements, and GEO readiness scoring. A clear starting point, whether you work with me or implement independently." },
];

const different = [
  { title: 'Answer-first content architecture.', body: "In CXL's analysis of 100 AI Overview citations, 55% of the quoted passages came from the first 30% of the page. I structure your pages so the most important information appears where both humans and machines look first." },
  { title: 'Citation-ready formatting.', body: "AI models extract information more reliably from clear headings, structured lists, and concise factual statements. I design content that's easy for machines to quote accurately." },
  { title: 'Verifiable trust signals.', body: "Google's quality guidelines centre on E-E-A-T (Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, Trustworthiness), and Google's AI answers draw on the same ranking systems. I build these signals into your content with author attribution, original data, cited sources and named client results." },
  { title: 'Technical AI readiness.', body: 'I check that AI crawlers can read your pages without running JavaScript and that nothing stops Google showing them in AI answers. I also make sure your Google Business Profile and directory listings match your site.' },
];

const sectors = ['Professional Services', 'Trade', 'Property', 'Tech & Engineering', 'SaaS', 'Healthcare', 'Legal'];

const faq = [
  { q: 'How much does SEO cost?', a: 'My day rate is £500. A short audit with a list of priority fixes takes half a day and costs £250. A full SEO and GEO audit usually takes two days, so it starts at about £1,000, and larger sites with more keywords or audiences take longer. Ongoing SEO and GEO starts at £500 a month, which buys one day of my time. For comparison, UK price guides published in 2026 put most small-business SEO at £500 to £5,000 a month, nearly all of it agency retainers. With me, the fee pays for my hours on your site, with no account manager or agency overhead on top.' },
  { q: 'What makes local (Aberdeen) SEO different from general SEO?', a: "Local SEO requires understanding local search behaviour, specific sector terminology, and the B2B buying cycle typical of Scottish companies. Optimising your Google Business Profile, building local citations in Aberdeen, Scottish business directories or even global ones, and earning industry-specific backlinks all play a role. Aberdeen's economy has specific characteristics (the energy sector transition, a growing technology cluster, and a dense professional services market) that shape what works." },
  { q: 'How long does SEO take to work?', a: 'Most Aberdeen businesses see measurable improvements in 3-4 months. Local SEO can show results faster (4-8 weeks) than national or global campaigns. Competitive keywords like "engineering services Aberdeen" may take 6-12 months. I have experienced instances where results can be achieved within weeks.' },
  { q: 'What does an SEO & GEO audit include?', a: 'A one-off assessment of how your website performs in Google and in AI answer engines. It covers the technical issues that stop pages ranking, content gaps against the searches your buyers use, your Google Business Profile and local listings, and whether AI tools can read and cite your pages. You get a prioritised action list you can implement yourself or with me. A short audit costs £250 and a full audit starts at about £1,000.' },
  { q: 'Can you guarantee results?', a: 'No one can guarantee #1 rankings, but I use proven strategies that consistently improve visibility and traffic for your business.' },
  { q: 'Should I hire an SEO consultant or an agency in Aberdeen?', a: 'It depends on the amount of work, not on which sounds bigger. An agency suits large sites that need several people producing content every week. A consultant suits SMEs that need senior judgement from the person doing the work. With me, the person who audits your site is the one who writes the pages and reports the results, with no account manager in between and no agency overhead in the fee.' },
  { q: 'What does an SEO consultant do?', a: "An SEO consultant works out why buyers aren't finding your site and then fixes it. In my case that means checking how Google and AI crawlers read your pages, writing or rewriting pages around what your buyers search for, earning links from sites in your sector, and making answers easy for AI Overviews and ChatGPT to quote. Each month I report what changed in Search Console and Analytics. How the time splits depends on the audit: some sites need mostly technical fixes, others need new pages." },
  { q: 'Is SEO worth it for a small business?', a: "It is if your buyers search for what you sell. Check that first: Google Search Console shows which searches already bring you impressions, and a keyword tool shows how many people search each month. For B2B firms in Aberdeen those numbers are often small, sometimes under a hundred searches a month, but in technical B2B one new client can be worth more than a year of SEO fees. SEO is a poor fit when almost nobody searches for the service, for example a product so new that buyers don't have a name for it yet. In that case events, LinkedIn and direct outreach will usually reach them sooner." },
  { q: 'Is SEO dead in 2026?', a: `No, but the payoff has changed. AI Overviews, AI Mode and ChatGPT search build their answers from pages they can crawl and index, and <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features" class="text-link">Google's guidance on AI features</a> says the usual SEO practices still apply. What has dropped is the click. The work now has two parts: getting the page to rank, and writing it so AI tools quote it and name you as the source. I cover what still works in <a href="/journal/seo-in-2025-what-works-whats-hype-what-fails/" class="text-link">SEO in 2025: what works, what's hype, what fails</a>.` },
  { q: 'How do I choose an SEO company in Aberdeen?', a: "Ask for named results: which clients, which searches, and what changed. Ask whether they looked at your Search Console data before quoting, because a plan built without it is a package. Ask how they handle AI search too. Anyone selling llms.txt files or special AI markup as the answer is selling something Google says its AI features don't need. Then ask to speak to a current client." },
  { q: 'What is GEO and how does it affect business?', a: "Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO) is the practice of structuring your website content so that AI-powered search tools (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Google Gemini, Microsoft Copilot) cite your business in their generated answers. As more B2B buyers use these tools to research suppliers, businesses that aren't optimised for AI search will lose visibility to competitors who are. GEO is particularly relevant in professional services and technology sectors, where buyers increasingly ask AI tools for recommendations before contacting providers." },
  { q: 'Do I need GEO if I already have SEO?', a: 'SEO and GEO are complementary, not competing. Good SEO gives you the foundation: fast site, clean structure, relevant content. GEO builds on that foundation by ensuring your content is formatted so AI engines can reliably extract and cite it. If your current SEO is solid, adding GEO optimisation is a relatively low-effort upgrade with significant upside as AI search adoption grows.' },
  { q: 'How do you measure GEO success?', a: 'GEO performance is measured through three metrics: mention rate (how often AI engines reference your brand by name), citation rate (how often they include a clickable link to your site), and citation position (where your brand appears in the generated answer, whether first, middle, or last). I also track which specific queries trigger citations and how that changes over time. These metrics are still maturing across the industry, but early measurement is how you build an advantage.' },
];

const posts = [
  { category: 'Industry insights', title: "What Google's Antitrust Trial Revealed About Ranking", href: '/journal/google-antitrust-documents-seo/' },
  { category: 'Digital marketing', title: 'The 2026 Blueprint to AI Agent Commerce: Getting Your Products Bought (instead of just discovered)', href: '/journal/the-2026-blueprint-to-ai-agent-commerce-getting-your-products-bought-instead-of-just-discovered/' },
  { category: 'Digital marketing', title: 'Is Your Content Ready for the AI Search Revolution?', href: '/journal/is-your-content-ready-for-the-ai-search-revolution/' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Service',
      name: 'SEO Aberdeen: SEO and GEO services',
      description: 'Traditional search engine optimisation combined with Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO) for businesses in Aberdeen and Scotland.',
      provider: { '@type': 'Person', '@id': `${origin}/#person`, name: 'Yann Hamonou' },
      areaServed: [
        { '@type': 'City', name: 'Aberdeen' },
        { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Aberdeenshire' },
        { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Scotland' },
      ],
      serviceType: 'SEO Consultancy',
      hasOfferCatalog: {
        '@type': 'OfferCatalog',
        name: 'SEO & GEO services',
        itemListElement: [
          { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'SEO & GEO audit' }, price: '1000', priceCurrency: 'GBP' },
          { '@type': 'Offer', itemOffered: { '@type': 'Service', name: 'Ongoing SEO & GEO' }, price: '500', priceCurrency: 'GBP' },
        ],
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '') } })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="Aberdeen SEO | AEO/GEO Consultant for B2B companies in Scotland"
  exactTitle
  description="Aberdeen SEO consultant combining traditional SEO with AI search optimisation (GEO). Audits from £1,000, ongoing from £500/month. Free consultation."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', item: `${Astro.site}` },
    { name: 'Services', item: `${Astro.site}services` },
    { name: 'SEO Aberdeen', item: `${Astro.site}services/seo-aberdeen` },
  ]}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

  <!-- ═══ HERO ═══ -->
  <PageHero
    label="SEO and GEO"
    title="SEO Aberdeen"
    lede="SEO services in Aberdeen for businesses that want more than rankings."
    image={serviceImages['seo-aberdeen']}
  >
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <Button href="#contact" size="lg" arrow>Book your SEO &amp; GEO audit</Button>
      <Button href="tel:+447853455816" size="lg" variant="outline"><Icon name="phone" class="size-4" /> Call me</Button>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <!-- ═══ INTRO ═══ -->
  <section class="bg-paper py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <Heading size="lg" class="max-w-[18ch]">Rank in search engines and AI answers with expert SEO &amp; GEO services</Heading>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <Text size="lg">
          SEO services in Aberdeen for businesses that want more than rankings. I combine traditional search engine optimisation with Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO), the practice of structuring your content so that AI-powered search tools like ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity cite your business in their answers. With 20+ years of senior marketing experience, I help businesses across Aberdeen and Scotland build visibility that works in both Google results and the AI-driven search landscape that's accompanying them.
        </Text>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ RESULTS ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-paper py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container>
      <Text size="sm" tone="secondary">Evidence</Text>
      <Heading size="lg" class="mt-4 max-w-[16ch]">Aberdeen SEO results I've delivered</Heading>
      <Text size="lg" class="mt-6">SEO claims are easy to make. Here's what the data shows:</Text>
      <ul class="mt-12">
        {results.map((r) => (
          <li class="grid gap-4 border-t border-ink py-8 last:border-b md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-6">
            <Heading as="h3" size="md" class="md:col-span-4">{r.client}</Heading>
            <div class="md:col-span-7 md:col-start-6">
              <Text>{r.body}</Text>
              {r.quote && <Text class="mt-4 border-l-2 border-signal pl-4 font-semibold">{r.quote}</Text>}
              <a href={r.href} class="text-link mt-4 inline-block text-sm">{r.linkLabel}</a>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ WHY ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-stone py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container>
      <Text size="sm" tone="secondary">Need convincing?</Text>
      <Heading size="xl" class="mt-4 max-w-[18ch]">Why Aberdeen businesses pick my SEO services</Heading>
      <Text size="lg" class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
        Unlike larger agencies, I provide hands-on, senior-level expertise without the overheads. Every strategy is built around your business goals, grounded in data, and designed for the reality of how people search today, not how they searched five years ago. That means optimising for Google and for the AI engines that are reshaping how buyers find providers.
      </Text>
      <ul class="mt-12 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-10 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {reasons.map((r) => (
          <li class="border-t border-ink pt-6">
            <Heading as="h3" size="sm">{r.title}</Heading>
            <Text class="mt-3 max-w-md">{r.body}</Text>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ SERVICES: numbered hairline rows ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-paper">
    <Container class="py-16 md:py-24">
      <Text size="sm" tone="secondary">Services</Text>
      <Heading size="lg" class="mt-4">SEO services in Aberdeen</Heading>
    </Container>
    <ol>
      {offer.map((o, i) => (
        <li class="border-t border-ink">
          <Container class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-5 gap-y-3 py-8 sm:gap-x-8 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-6 md:py-10">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-heading text-6xl font-extrabold leading-none tracking-[-0.05em] [font-stretch:110%] md:col-span-2">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div class="md:col-span-8">
              <Heading as="h3" size="md">{o.title}</Heading>
              <Text class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">{o.body}</Text>
            </div>
          </Container>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ SEO vs GEO ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-paper py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <Text size="sm" tone="secondary">How search is changing</Text>
        <Heading size="lg" class="mt-4">SEO vs GEO: why businesses need both</Heading>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-5 lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7">
        <Text size="lg">Google still sends nearly 90% of search referrals, and its AI Overviews and AI Mode build their answers from the same search index. SEO remains the foundation. What has changed is which pages get cited. In an analysis of about 4 million AI Overview citations (Ahrefs, March 2026), only 38% of cited pages ranked in the top 10 for the original search. Ahrefs' explanation is that the AI runs several related searches behind the scenes and cites pages that rank for those.</Text>
        <Text size="lg">GEO is the work of being one of those pages. In practice that means answering the specific questions your buyers ask, and being the business other sites already mention by name.</Text>
        <Text size="lg">Most of that work also improves your normal Google rankings, so it isn't a separate budget line. It doesn't need special markup or llms.txt files either. Google's guidance is that its AI features need nothing beyond good SEO (Google Search Central). Anyone selling you more should be able to show the evidence.</Text>
      </div>
    </Container>

    <Container class="mt-20">
      <Heading as="h3" size="md">What I do differently</Heading>
      <Text class="mt-4 max-w-2xl">Most SEO consultants optimise for Google's algorithm. I optimise for how both search engines and AI models evaluate trust and relevance. In practice, that means:</Text>
      <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-x-8">
        {different.map((d) => (
          <li class="border-t border-ink pt-6">
            <Text><strong class="font-semibold">{d.title}</strong> {d.body}</Text>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ WHO I WORK WITH ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-paper py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <Heading size="lg">Who I work with</Heading>
        <Text size="lg" class="mt-6 max-w-2xl">
          I work with Aberdeen companies across professional services, trades, property, and technology. These are businesses where the buyer's journey starts with a search, whether that's on Google or increasingly through an AI tool. Whether you need more local leads or want to compete nationally, I build SEO and GEO strategies around how your specific customers actually find and evaluate providers.
        </Text>
      </div>
      <Tag class="lg:col-span-3 lg:col-start-10">
        {sectors.map((s) => <span class="block">{s}</span>)}
      </Tag>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ CLIENT FEEDBACK ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-stone py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <Heading size="lg">Client feedback</Heading>
      </div>
      <figure class="lg:col-span-7 lg:col-start-6">
        <blockquote class="space-y-4">
          <Text size="lg">“Before working with Yann, we weren't generating enough inbound leads.</Text>
          <Text size="lg">Now when I ask prospects how they found us, the answer is always one of two things: either they've used Arnlea before at a previous company, or they searched for Ex or ATEX inspection software and we came up at the top of the results. That search visibility is new and has increased the number of new enquiries we receive. I've already recommended Yann to other companies I think he could help.”</Text>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 border-t border-ink pt-6">
          <div>
            <Text class="font-semibold">Claire Murray</Text>
            <Text size="sm" tone="secondary">Head of Business Development, Arnlea</Text>
          </div>
          <a href="/work/arnlea/" class="text-link text-sm">Read the case study</a>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ FAQ ═══ -->
  <section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-20 border-t border-ink bg-paper py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <Text size="sm" tone="secondary">Some questions you might have</Text>
        <Heading size="lg" class="mt-4">FAQs</Heading>
        <Text class="mt-6 max-w-sm">Things you need to know about my services. Can't find the answer you're looking for? <a href="#contact" class="text-link">Please reach out to me.</a></Text>
      </div>
      <dl class="lg:col-span-7 lg:col-start-6">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <div class="grid gap-3 border-t border-ink py-8 last:border-b md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.3fr)] md:gap-8">
            <dt><Heading as="h3" size="sm">{f.q}</Heading></dt>
            <dd><Text><Fragment set:html={f.a} /></Text></dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ JOURNAL ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-paper py-20 md:py-28">
    <Container>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between">
        <Heading size="lg">Blogs</Heading>
        <a href="/journal/" class="text-link text-sm">View all posts</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="mt-10">
        {posts.map((p) => (
          <li class="border-t border-ink last:border-b">
            <a href={p.href} class="group grid gap-2 py-6 md:grid-cols-12 md:items-center md:gap-6">
              <Text size="sm" tone="secondary" class="md:col-span-3">{p.category}</Text>
              <Heading as="h3" size="sm" class="decoration-signal decoration-2 underline-offset-4 group-hover:underline md:col-span-8">{p.title}</Heading>
              <Icon name="arrow-right" stroke={1} class="hidden size-8 justify-self-end transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 md:block" />
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ OTHER SERVICES: internal links ═══ -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink bg-paper py-14">
    <Container class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between">
      <Text size="sm" tone="secondary">Other services</Text>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        {otherServices.map((s) => <Button href={`/services/${s.slug}/`} variant="outline" size="sm">{s.title}</Button>)}
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ CLOSING ═══ -->
  <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-20 bg-signal py-20 text-ink md:py-28">
    <Container class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <Heading size="xl" tone="onAccent" class="max-w-[14ch]">SEO services in Aberdeen: get started today</Heading>
        <span class="mt-6 hidden lg:block"><Icon name="arrow-right" stroke={0.6} class="size-40" /></span>
        <Text size="lg" tone="onAccent" class="mt-8 max-w-md lg:mt-4">
          If you're ready to grow your business with an SEO and GEO strategy that's built for how search actually works today, let's talk. I offer a free initial consultation to assess your current visibility and identify the highest-impact opportunities.
        </Text>
        <Text tone="onAccent" class="mt-8"><a href="tel:+447853455816" class="underline underline-offset-4">Call today: +44 (0) 785 3455816</a></Text>
      </div>
      <ContactForm id="seo-contact" buttonLabel="Book your SEO & GEO audit" class="lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8 lg:self-start" />
    </Container>
  </section>
</Layout>
